From a1d28623b95b4c41bc4de32a699bbc89b053b3f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:56:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): route paced profile defaults through their own
 peers [daveey]

Problem: unpinned coach and alpha-follow class:standard cards stayed ready behind
an xai-oauth reserve hold for about 67 hours despite available class peers.
Why 1: pacing expands fallback class providers from the dispatcher's effective
config, not the assignee's registry (kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch.class_providers).
Why 2: the alternate probe explicitly refused tier-off/out-of-scope routes.
Root (happened): claim-time offer custody only matched tier-selected routes;
profile fallback routes were not consumed against their actual launch route.
Root (not caught): the old regression deliberately asserted a hold to avoid
launching on a held route after dropping an offer. Queue placement also returned
before reading the pacing skip, hiding it behind worker placement wording.
Recurrence: extends the prior pace-offer custody fix (review 5912306106) rather
than removing that safety check.

Bind profile offers to the effective route at application, enumerate eligible
providers from the assignee's class registry, and preserve credential/wall checks.
Explicit pins keep their reserve hold rather than taking a far-pacing peer.
Read the latest pacing skip before placement and expose its provider/reset note.
No pacing reserves, budgets or priorities change.

Proof: baseline profile fixture: 4 failures, then GREEN; queue fixture: 4 RED
failures, then GREEN. Focused routing/reviewer/queue suite: 116 tests passed.
Full consumer/check gates and independent exact-head review remain required.
